PART 4: Amplitude Analysis — Why Composite Peaks Are Suppressed
========================================================================

eps = phi^(-1)/4 = 0.154508
3*eps = 0.463525

Fibonacci ladder P_m = 3*eps*F_m*phi^(-2(m-1)):
  m |  F_m |  phi^(-2(m-1)) |        P_m |      A_obs |    ratio
------------------------------------------------------------
  1 |    1 |       1.000000 |   0.463525 |        --- |      ---
  2 |    1 |       0.381966 |   0.177051 |        --- |      ---
  3 |    2 |       0.145898 |   0.135255 |        --- |      ---
  4 |    3 |       0.055728 |   0.077494 |        --- |      ---
  5 |    5 |       0.021286 |   0.049334 |        --- |      ---
  6 |    8 |       0.008131 |   0.030150 |        --- |      ---
  7 |   13 |       0.003106 |   0.018714 |        --- |      ---

The key insight: composite m=4,6 have amplitudes SIMILAR to
m=5,7 respectively. The suppression is NOT in the amplitude
but in the PEAK DETECTION — the peaks are at the wrong positions
and blend into the damping tail.

